src/dsv41/ds4_kernels.cu: in-kernel stage markers for route_publish_kernel (K100AI, DEBUG ONLY).

The launch probe (patches/0002) named route_publish_kernel as the launch in flight when the
process dies, but not how far the kernel got.  This adds 13 progress slots plus two counters:

   0 entered            5 winner written        10 req->ids / req->w written
   1 preload done       6 top-k loop finished   11 on_cpu set
   2 after barrier      7 denominator done      12 after the last barrier
   3 top-k round r      8 before pick r writes  14 invocations started
   4 in winner block    9 idx/w/plan_ptr done   15 invocations finished

The slots live in host-mapped memory (cudaHostAlloc(Mapped), which the DCU can be written by the
GPU - verified with a micro-test) and a host thread copies them to
/4T-02/strata-work/ds4_markers.bin every 2 ms.  A VM fault kills the process, the file survives.

The patch also carries the DS4_NO_REQ_X switch (the req->x bulk host write), which the negative
experiment needed; it defaults to on, i.e. unchanged behaviour.

Do not ship: a fence per marker and a 2 ms writer thread.

